============================================================
WHERE DOES THE PACKET WAIT WHEN TX QUEUE IS STOPPED?
============================================================

There are TWO different waiting places.
Which one is used depends on HOW FAR the packet has progressed
in the networking stack.


============================================================
3) CASE A: Packet has NOT reached dev_queue_xmit()
============================================================

--- Layer
    Layer 4 (TCP / UDP)

--- TCP case
    Packet is stored in:

        struct sock
            └── sk_write_queue

    Reasons this happens:
        - Congestion window (cwnd) full
        - Receiver advertised window closed
        - Nagle algorithm enabled
        - TCP corking
        - TCP pacing

    Notes:
        - Packet has NOT reached IP output yet
        - No L2 header added
        - No qdisc involved
        - NO relation to TX queue stop
        - netif_tx_stop_queue() is NOT visible here


--- UDP case
    Packet may briefly be stored in:

        struct sock
            └── sk_write_queue

    Notes:
        - UDP usually pushes packets quickly to IP
        - Minimal buffering compared to TCP
        - Still unrelated to TX queue stop


============================================================
4) CASE B: Packet HAS reached dev_queue_xmit()
============================================================

--- Stack position
    Below Layer 3 (IP)
    Layer 2 / netdevice layer

--- Call flow
    ip_local_out()
        ↓
    ip_output()
        ↓
    dev_queue_xmit()


--- Inside dev_queue_xmit()
    1) Selects qdisc (pfifo_fast, fq, fq_codel, etc.)
    2) Enqueues skb into qdisc queue
    3) Attempts to dequeue skb
    4) Attempts to call ndo_start_xmit()


--- TX queue stopped case
    Condition:
        Driver has called:

            netif_tx_stop_queue(txq)

    Result:
        - qdisc will NOT call ndo_start_xmit()
        - skb remains queued in qdisc
        - skb is NOT returned to TCP
        - skb is NOT stored in sk_write_queue


--- Packet state here
    - skb is fully formed
        * L4 header present
        * IP header present
        * Ethernet header present
    - Routing already done
    - Neighbor resolution already done
    - Layer 4 is completely out of the picture


============================================================
SUMMARY
============================================================

- Layer 4 buffering:
    Location:
        sk->sk_write_queue
    Reason:
        TCP/UDP flow control
    Relation to TX queue stop:
        NONE

- Netdevice buffering:
    Location:
        qdisc queue
    Reason:
        TX queue stopped (hardware/DMA full)
    Relation to TX queue stop:
        DIRECT

- TX queue stop is checked ONLY in:
    dev_queue_xmit() / qdisc layer

- TCP/UDP NEVER know:
    - netdev_tx_queue
    - TX ring state
    - DMA descriptor availability

